  "decision": null,
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The office floorspace at first floor level, hereby approved,\r\n    shall not be occupied until the alterations to the external\r\n    elevations at ground floor level (excluding future tenant's\r\n    shopfronts) and other works required to make the premises\r\n    ready for future tenants use shall have been completed\r\n    in accordance with details which shall have been submitted\r\n    to and approved by the Council, and the floorspace made\r\n    ready for occupation.",
    "Condition : 2 - Details of the wind shelf shall not be otherwise than shall\r\n    have been submitted to and approved by the Council before\r\n    any work on the site, with respect to the wind shelf, is\r\n    commenced",
    "Condition : 3 - The whole of the landscaping shown on drawing 1946 SK 101\r\n    shall have been completed by the end of the first planting\r\n    season following occupation of the floorspace hereby\r\n    permitted.",
    "Condition : 4 - The ground floor of the building shall not be used other\r\n    than for uses within Classes A or D (Town and Country\r\n    Planning (Use Classes Order) 1987), with the west side of\r\n    the ground floor being used only for Class A1(retail) or\r\n    A3(restaurant) use",
    "Condition : 5 - Details of servicing arrangements for any retail use at\r\n    ground floor level shall be submitted to and approved by the\r\n    Council before that particular use commences",
    "Condition : 6 - The use hereby permitted shall not begin until full details of the scheme for the ventilation of and the extraction of fumes from the premises to an adequate outlet level, including details of sound attenuation for any necessary plant have been submitted to and approved by the Council and the development shall not be carried out otherwise than in accordance with any approval given.\r\n\r\nReason: To safeguard the amenities of the [adjoining] premises [and the area generally] in accordance with the requirements of policy[ies] RE2[, EN5, EN6, DS6 (and SH18 if A3 use)] of the London Borough of Camden Unitary Development Plan 2000.\r\n",
    "Condition : 7 - Before the use commences, details of the method of storage and waste removal (including recycled materials) shall be submitted to and approved by the Council and the approved method shall thereafter be maintained.\r\n\r\nReason: To safeguard the amenities of the [adjoining] premises [and the area generally] in accordance with the requirements of policy[ies] RE2[, EN5, EN6, DS6 (and SH18 if A3 use)] of the London Borough of Camden Unitary Development Plan 2000.\r\n",
    "Condition : 8 - In order to ensure that the development is completed and\r\n    occupied as permitted.",
    "Condition : 9 - In order to ensure the development is completed as\r\n    permitted.",
    "Condition : 10 - In order to ensure the entire development is completed as\r\n    permitted.",
    "Condition : 11 - To ensure the ground floor is used for an appropriate mix of\r\n    uses.",
    "Condition : 12 - To avoid obstruction of the surrounding streets and to\r\n    safeguard amenities of adjacent premises.",
    "Condition : 13 - To safeguard the amenities of the adjoining premises and the\r\n    area generally.",
    "Condition : 14 - To safeguard the amenities of the adjoining premises and the\r\n    area generally.",
    "Condition : 15 - The details required pursuant to additional conditions 1, 2,\r\n    5, 6 & 7 should be submitted with the attached approval of\r\n    details application form together with 5 sets of drawings\r\n    and any other supporting information."
  ],
